# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# inventory-api environment variables (specs/015-hardware-inventory)
#
# DATA RESIDENCY — MANDATORY constraints (CLAUDE.md):
#   1. EU region: this service MUST be deployed to an EU region only.
#      Production target: Railway EU (europe-west4), see railway.json. No
#      asset, ledger or assignment data (financial figures, who holds which
#      device) may be stored outside the EU — this includes the invoice-file
#      bucket below.
#   2. No body logging: request/response bodies must NEVER appear in
#      application logs. Only method + path + status are logged
#      (src/lib/logger.ts). Do NOT add a logger that includes bodies, query
#      strings or the Prisma 'query' log level.
#
# Every variable below is validated at startup in src/lib/env.ts
# (`process.exit(1)` on any missing or invalid value). Copy this file to
# `.env` (gitignored) or load it through direnv; NEVER commit real secrets.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ─── CORS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated allowed origins, no wildcards. inventory-ui is a federated
# remote reached through the shell (ADR-0006), so the shell origin is the one
# that matters; 5178 is inventory-ui's own pinned dev port.
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,http://localhost:5178

# ─── Auth (JWT resource-server verification, ADR-0005/0010) ──────────────────
# Use /auth/jwks (better-auth's DB-backed keyset), NOT /.well-known/jwks.json —
# see refund-api/.env.example for the full story.
AUTH_JWKS_URL=http://localhost:3001/auth/jwks
AUTH_ISSUER=http://localhost:3001

# auth base URL: GET /authz/resolve (live permissions, ADR-0014),
# POST /authz/users/identities (display names, ADR-0039) and
# POST /system/service-token (ADR-0044).
AUTH_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3001

# Suite-wide JWT audience (ADR-0010) — a single constant, identical in
# auth/.env.example and every resource server.
AUTH_AUDIENCE=operai-suite

# ─── Server ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 8083 — estimai-api 8080, notify-api 8081, refund-api 8082.
PORT=8083
NODE_ENV=development

# ─── Invoice-file object storage (ADR-0016 posture) ──────────────────────────
# An EU-region, S3-compatible, PRIVATE bucket — its own bucket and credentials,
# never refund-api's. Reached only through presigned URLs.
#
# EU-RESIDENCY GUARD IS ENDPOINT-AWARE (same rule as refund-api, OWASP A05):
#   - endpoint host `*.amazonaws.com`  -> INVENTORY_S3_REGION must be an EU AWS
#     region (eu-west-1/2/3, eu-central-1/2, eu-north-1, eu-south-1/2);
#   - any other host (Railway, MinIO, …) -> the region string is an opaque SDK
#     placeholder, so residency is enforced against
#     INVENTORY_S3_EU_ENDPOINT_HOSTS. Empty/unset/non-matching = exit 1.
#
# Local dev against the compose MinIO (see compose.yaml) is:
#   INVENTORY_S3_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:9000
#   INVENTORY_S3_REGION=us-east-1
#   INVENTORY_S3_BUCKET=operai-inventory-invoices-dev
#   INVENTORY_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=minioadmin
#   INVENTORY_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=minioadmin
#   INVENTORY_S3_EU_ENDPOINT_HOSTS=localhost
# The values below are placeholders for a deployed EU bucket.
REFUND_S3_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:9000
INVENTORY_S3_REGION=auto
INVENTORY_S3_BUCKET=operai-inventory-invoices-dev
INVENTORY_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=minioadmin
INVENTORY_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=minioadmin
INVENTORY_S3_EU_ENDPOINT_HOSTS=s3.railway-eu-amsterdam.example.com

# ─── notify-api push (best-effort, after commit) ─────────────────────────────
# POST /system/notifications, authenticated with a scoped service JWT minted by
# auth (plan § Service authentication) — NOT NOTIFY_INTERNAL_TOKEN (ADR-0040).
# Local: notify-api's dev port. Production: notify-api's PRIVATE-networking
# address (e.g. http://notify-api.railway.internal:8081), never its public
# domain.
NOTIFY_INTERNAL_URL=http://localhost:8081

# ─── Service credential for auth POST /system/service-token (ADR-0044) ───────
# SERVICE_CLIENT_ID must match an entry of auth's SERVICE_CLIENTS and carry the
# `notifications.push` scope. SERVICE_CLIENT_SECRET must be >= 32 chars and
# byte-identical to that entry's secret; generate with `openssl rand -hex 32`.
SERVICE_CLIENT_ID=inventory-api
SERVICE_CLIENT_SECRET=change-me-to-a-random-string-of-at-least-32-characters
